## Part 2: Decision

Apply this rubric and recommend one option. Show which findings drive the choice.

- Cross-release logic (1.2): a few isolated cases favors A; move them into the product chart or into static data. Wiring that many releases consume favors B.
- .gotmpl buckets (3): if most files are bucket A or B, conversion is mechanical and favors A. If bucket C logic is common outside the global templates and Airflow, estimate the effort before committing to A.
- Deploy-time inputs (2): under A or B, every env var, exec or readFile that varies per environment must become data in git. Count them; a long list raises effort for both.
- CLI duties (5): every duty needs a named replacement (Argo, CI, Kargo, or dropped). Any duty with no home is a blocker to resolve first.
- Non-deterministic functions (8.3) and lookup: these must be fixed under A or B either way.
- Secrets (9): if SOPS must stay in git, B is simpler short-term. Moving to External Secrets fits A.
- Client handoff: if clients must install without Argo, the charts and static values must stay usable with plain Helm or a thin Helmfile.

